WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
Two flat metal plates face each
other across a thin gap of air.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.860
Connect them to a 12 volt supply.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.560
Charge flows on, then stops.

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:13.490
Each plate now holds
just 4.2 nanocoulombs.

5
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.290
You want more, but the supply is fixed.

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.960
How can you get more charge onto the
capacitor without raising the voltage?

7
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:25.760
In this mission, you'll find out what sets
the capacitance of two parallel plates,

8
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.520
and what has no effect on it at all.

9
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.210
Then you'll meet a capacitor that holds
far more charge than its size suggests,

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.770
and find out why.

11
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.510
Your mission: find a way to get more
charge onto the capacitor without raising

12
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.440
the voltage.
